  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal, both in itself and when seen in conjunction with the previous extensions to the property, would be unacceptable in design terms and represent an excessively scaled form of development that would not appear subordinate to the original dwelling, resulting in harm to the character and appearance of the property itself and the wider area contrary to Local Plan policies CC1, CC2 and SC7 as well as the council's design guidance",
    "Reason : 2 - Due to the excessive depth the proposal would result in a loss of outlook and an increased sense of enclosure for neighbouring occupiers to the detriment of their living conditions and contrary to Local Plan policies CC1, CC2 and SC7 as well as the council's design guidance",
    "Reason : 3 - The height of front boundary treatment would result in harm to the pedestrian and highway safety contrary to London Plan policy T4 and Local Plan EC2 as well as the council's guidance"
  ],
